# Package overlay working areas (PROPOSED_SPEC_CHANGES.md revision 2,
# "Automatic Classification, Flat Working Directory").
#
# A package directory's working area (packages/<pkg>/<flat files mirroring
# upstream paths>) is local editing scratch, regenerated into patches/ and
# files/ by `refresh` — it must never be committed. patches/, files/, the
# per-package refresh manifest, and .pkgignore ARE the checked-in artifacts
# and must stay tracked.
#
# .pkgignore is metadata, not scratch: it decides what `refresh` classifies at
# all, so a clone without it regenerates every ignored doc back into files/.
#
# This file is scoped to packages/ only — it does not touch the top-level
# .gitignore (an upstream file) and has no effect on packages/forth-core/'s
# pre-existing, already-tracked files (ignore rules never affect files git
# already tracks).
# Design docs are source, not scratch, and unlike the working-area sources they
# have no generated counterpart to be tracked through: .pkgignore deliberately
# keeps *.md/*.txt OUT of patches/ and files/, so a doc that is not tracked here
# is tracked nowhere and exists only on one disk. (A working-area .c is safe to
# ignore precisely because refresh regenerates it into files/ or patches/.)
# Without these two lines every doc added after this rule landed — DESIGN-HISTORY.md,
# the review series, the architect reports — was silently invisible to git, while
# the docs predating it stayed tracked. Ignore rules never affect already-tracked
# files, so the trap only sprang on new ones.
*/*
!*/patches
!*/patches/**
!*/files
!*/files/**
!*/.refresh-manifest.json
!*/.pkgignore
!*/*.md
!*/*.txt
